# QEMU system emulation targets that ::gentoo does not describe yet.
#
# This file is additive: Portage and pkgcheck read profiles/desc/ from every
# repository in the stack and merge them, so only the targets missing from
# ::gentoo belong here.  Everything else keeps coming from
# gentoo/profiles/desc/qemu_softmmu_targets.desc.
#
# hexagon gained system emulation in QEMU 11.1 -- the release ships
# configs/targets/hexagon-softmmu.mak alongside the long-standing
# hexagon-linux-user.mak.  ::gentoo still lists hexagon only under
# qemu_user_targets (its qemu-9999 keeps it in IUSE_USER_TARGETS), so without
# this entry pkgcheck reports UnknownUseFlags for qemu_softmmu_targets_hexagon
# and the flag would be invisible to users of this overlay.
#
# Drop this file once ::gentoo describes the flag itself.
hexagon - Qualcomm Hexagon system emulation target
